# /etc/nut/upssched.conf
#
# FIX: CMDSCRIPT must point at a path the `nut` user can actually reach. The
# previous deployment pointed under /home (0700, unreadable by `nut`) AND at a
# non-existent lowercase "python" dir, so every event silently no-opped. The
# dispatcher is installed to /usr/local/bin by deploy/install.sh.
#
# Notification-only model: each event is forwarded to the orchestrator. The
# actual protective shutdown is handled by upsmon's SHUTDOWNCMD, not here.

CMDSCRIPT /usr/local/bin/upssched-cmd.sh
PIPEFN /run/nut/upssched.pipe
LOCKFN /run/nut/upssched.lock

# Debounced ONBATT (applies to every UPS, *): a real outage only alerts if the
# UPS stays on battery past a short grace, so sub-15s utility dips don't page.
#
#   ONBATT -> start a 15s timer named `onbatt_grace`.
#   ONLINE -> CANCEL-TIMER onbatt_grace online
#             NUT semantics: if the timer is still counting (brief dip), it is
#             cancelled and nothing runs — silent. If it already FIRED (the
#             outage was real and `onbatt` was sent), the optional `online`
#             command runs, so the restore alert only follows a real outage.
#
# When the timer fires, upssched invokes CMDSCRIPT with `onbatt_grace`, which the
# dispatcher forwards to the orchestrator's `onbatt` handler.
AT ONBATT  * START-TIMER onbatt_grace 15
AT ONLINE  * CANCEL-TIMER onbatt_grace online

# LOWBATT is critical — never debounced.
AT LOWBATT * EXECUTE lowbatt
AT COMMBAD * EXECUTE commbad
AT COMMOK  * EXECUTE commok
